# Pre-push quality gate

Before committing or pushing changes in this repo:

1. Run `npm test` — all unit tests must pass.
2. Run `npm run build` — production build must succeed.
3. Or run `npm run ci` to execute both.

## When tests are required

- Any change under `src/calculations/`, `src/utils/`, or `tests/`
- Any change that alters mortgage math, payment scenarios, or investment comparison
- UI changes that depend on calculation outputs (results display, charts, scenarios)

## If behavior intentionally changes

- Update the affected tests in `tests/` to match the new expected values.
- Never delete tests to make CI pass without user approval.
- Document why baseline values changed in the commit message.

## Do not push when

- `npm test` fails
- `npm run build` fails
- Calculation logic was modified without corresponding test updates
